flowchart LR
  subgraph CONTROL["1. GitHub Actions · release control"]
    direction TB
    CI["release_experiments.py<br/>Run tests · collect decisions<br/>Request promotion · detect failure · recover"]
  end

  subgraph CLIENT["2. Client EC2"]
    direction TB
    TEST["Test client<br/>release_worker.py · tls_handshake.c<br/>Select route and make real TLS connection"]
    RECORD["Per-connection records<br/>Negotiation · certificate · timing · result"]
    TEST --> RECORD
  end

  subgraph SERVER["3. Server EC2 · lab TLS services"]
    direction TB
    WORKER["Server-side test workers<br/>release_worker.py · gate_worker.py<br/>Evaluate crypto, certificate and performance<br/>Start candidate · update route state"]
    POLICY["Policy files<br/>pqc-required.json<br/>release-slo.json"]
    STATE["route.json<br/>Backend ports for active · candidate · rollback<br/>New connections only; existing sessions stay"]
    ROUTER["Lab TCP router<br/>External port :4433<br/>Relays bytes; does not terminate TLS"]
    ACTIVE["active server process<br/>Initial port :24430<br/>Initially: X25519 + ECDSA P-256<br/>After approval: KPQC service"]
    CANDIDATE["candidate server process<br/>KPQC candidate<br/>Separate port :24431 and above"]
    PREVIOUS["Previously approved KPQC process<br/>Kept for recovery after a later update"]
    POLICY -->|Read criteria| WORKER
    WORKER -->|Write route state| STATE
    STATE -->|Router reads route state| ROUTER
    ROUTER -->|active destination| ACTIVE
    ROUTER -->|candidate destination| CANDIDATE
    ROUTER -.->|rollback destination| PREVIOUS
  end

  CI -. SSH test commands .-> TEST
  CI -. SSH commands · evidence · decision request .-> WORKER
  WORKER -. Return decision .-> CI
  TEST -->|"Send selector first<br/>active or candidate · lab-only plaintext"| ROUTER
  RECORD -. Collect evidence for decision .-> CI

